## Identify a, b and c
Compare with $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$: $a = 3$, $b = -2$, $c = -4$.
## Substitute into the quadratic formula
x &= \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
&= \frac{-(-2) \pm \sqrt{(-2)^2 - 4(3)(-4)}}{2(3)}
&= \frac{2 \pm \sqrt{4 + 48}}{6}
&= \frac{2 \pm \sqrt{52}}{6}
## Work out the two roots to 2 decimal places
x &= \frac{2 + \sqrt{52}}{6}
&\approx 1.54
x &= \frac{2 - \sqrt{52}}{6}
&\approx -0.87
ANSWER: x = 1.54 \text{ or } x = -0.87

## Write 58 000 as a number between 1 and 10 times a power of 10
Put the decimal point after the first digit: $5.8$. It moved 4 places, so the power is $4$.
58\,000 &= 5.8 \times 10\,000
&= 5.8 \times 10^{4}
## Write 0.036 as a number between 1 and 10 times a power of 10
Put the decimal point after the first non-zero digit: $3.6$. It moved 2 places to the right, so the power is $-2$.
0.036 &= 3.6 \times \frac{1}{100}
&= 3.6 \times 10^{-2}
ANSWER: 58\,000 = 5.8 \times 10^{4},\quad 0.036 = 3.6 \times 10^{-2}

## Split the 12 ranked values into a lower and upper half
There are 12 values, so the lower half is the first 6: $42, 64, 93, 94, 114, 114$.
## Find Q1 as the median of the lower half
The median of 6 values is the mean of the 3rd and 4th values: $93$ and $94$.
Q_1 &= \frac{93+94}{2}
&= \frac{187}{2}
&= 93.5 \text{ mm}
## Subtract to get the interquartile range
\text{IQR} &= Q_3 - Q_1
&= 183 - 93.5
&= 89.5 \text{ mm}
ANSWER: Q_1 = 93.5 \text{ mm}, \quad \text{IQR} = 89.5 \text{ mm}

## Choose the right ratio
$x$ is opposite the $30^\circ$ angle and $10$ cm is adjacent to it, so use tangent.
\tan 30^\circ &= \frac{x}{10}
## Solve for x
x &= 10 \tan 30^\circ
x &= 5.7735...
x &= 5.77 \text{ cm}
ANSWER: x = 5.77 \text{ cm}

## Find the angle at Q
The angles of a triangle add to $180^\circ$.
\angle Q &= 180 - (104 + 41)
&= 35^\circ
## Write the sine rule
$|PR|$ is opposite the $35^\circ$ angle and $11$ cm is opposite the $104^\circ$ angle.
\frac{|PR|}{\sin 35^\circ} &= \frac{11}{\sin 104^\circ}
## Solve for |PR|
|PR| &= \frac{11 \sin 35^\circ}{\sin 104^\circ}
&= 6.502...
&= 6.5 \text{ cm}
ANSWER: |PR| = 6.5 \text{ cm}

## Use the slope formula
$A(-5,3)$ and $B(2,0)$. Slope $= \frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}$, taking $B$ as the second point.
m &= \frac{0-3}{2-(-5)}
&= \frac{-3}{2+5}
&= -\frac{3}{7}
ANSWER: m = -\frac{3}{7}

## Find the slope of l
$l$ is in the form $y = mx + c$, so the slope is the number in front of $x$.
y &= \frac{2}{3}x - 5
m_l &= \frac{2}{3}
## Rearrange k into y = mx + c
2x + 3y - 7 &= 0
3y &= -2x + 7
y &= -\frac{2}{3}x + \frac{7}{3}
m_k &= -\frac{2}{3}
## Compare the slopes
Parallel lines have equal slopes. Perpendicular lines have slopes that multiply to $-1$.
m_l \times m_k &= \frac{2}{3} \times \left(-\frac{2}{3}\right)
&= -\frac{4}{9}
The slopes are not equal and the product is not $-1$, so tick "neither".
ANSWER: \text{neither}
